<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Lao People's Democratic Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1975 CE – present · capital Vientiane</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Communist Laos, a one-party state led by the Lao People's Revolutionary Party since the abolition of the monarchy in 1975.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a> gained control of the coalition government formed under the 1973 accords, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savang-vatthana">King Savang Vatthana</a> abdicated, and on 2 December 1975 the Lao People's Democratic Republic was proclaimed in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Vientiane</a>, with Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souphanouvong">Souphanouvong</a> as president and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaysone-phomvihane">Kaysone Phomvihane</a> as prime minister.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lao-peoples-revolutionary-party">Lao People's Revolutionary Party</a> rules as the only legal party, closely allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Early policies of collectivisation, re-education camps and suppression of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hmong-people">Hmong</a> resistance drove many to flee. From 1986 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-economic-mechanism">New Economic Mechanism</a> opened the economy to markets and foreign investment. Unexploded ordnance from the US bombing campaign still kills and injures people.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The Lao PDR continues today, joining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/association-of-southeast-asian-nations">ASEAN</a> in 1997. Growth from hydropower dams and mining, and the Chinese-built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boten-vientiane-railway">Laos-China railway</a> opened in 2021, have deepened ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, alongside heavy public debt.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lao-peoples-democratic-republic.jpg" alt="Lao People's Democratic Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Laos.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1975 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vientiane</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Souphanouvong, Kaysone Phomvihane, Thongloun Sisoulith</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lao</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/laos">Laos</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Laos, Lao PDR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2000&amp;focus=lao-peoples-democratic-republic" aria-label="Lao People's Democratic Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7464 1511 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lao People's Democratic Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7784 1767L7784 1767"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7784 1767h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vientiane. <a href="/atlas?year=2000&amp;focus=lao-peoples-democratic-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
